,[296,1104,627],{"class":306},[296,1106,1107],{"class":349},"unRegister",[296,1109,1110],{"class":310},"(identifier)\n",[270,1112,1113,1114,1116,1117,1120,1121,1123,1124,1126],{},"The zone is the complete zone the service lives in: ",[274,1115,547],{}," and ",[274,1118,1119],{},"defaultZone"," apply to ",[274,1122,276],{}," classes only. Registering the same identifier twice on one client is a no-op, and ",[274,1125,1107],{}," ends any stream the service is still producing with an error to its caller.",[282,1128,1130],{"id":1129},"the-service-directory","The service directory",[270,1132,1133,1134,1137,1138,1116,1141,1144,1145,1148,1149,1152,1153,1155,1156,1159,1160,1163,1164,1167,1168,1170],{},"Every published class under the project's ",[274,1135,1136],{},"servicesPaths"," gets a service definition from ",[274,1139,1140],{},"kinotic generate",[274,1142,1143],{},"kinotic sync",", its functions with their parameters and types, written to the ",[274,1146,1147],{},"ServiceDefinitions"," module under ",[274,1150,1151],{},"generatedPath",". A project that imports that module has the runtime register each service in the platform's service directory as the service comes online: the services registered before ",[274,1154,964],{}," when the client connects, and a service registered on a connected client as it registers. Only a service in an application's zone, ",[274,1157,1158],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>"," or a zone under it, is registered, through the platform's ",[274,1161,1162],{},"ApplicationServiceDirectory"," in ",[274,1165,1166],{},"app-api",", which refuses a zone that is not the application's or an application outside the caller's organization. The directory then holds the application's services beside the platform's own, with their liveness; a service the project declares no definition for serves on its zone alone. A definition naming other functions than the class serves fails the registration, and with it the connection, until ",[274,1169,1143],{}," runs again.",[1172,1173,1175],"h3",{"id":1174},"parameter-and-return-types","Parameter and return types",[270,1177,1178],{},"Arguments and results travel as JSON, so a function's types are published as JSON carries them:",[1180,1181,1182,1198,1208,1229,1238,1251],"ul",{},[1183,1184,1185,1186,1189,1190,1193,1194,1197],"li",{},"A ",[274,1187,1188],{},"Promise"," or ",[274,1191,1192],{},"PromiseLike"," result is asynchronous and an ",[274,1195,1196],{},"Observable"," result is a stream, of the type it resolves to or emits.",[1183,1199,1200,1203,1204,1207],{},[274,1201,1202],{},"any",", ",[274,1205,1206],{},"unknown",", and a type parameter with no constraint accept anything; a constrained type parameter is its constraint.",[1183,1209,1210,1211,1214,1215,1116,1218,1221,1222,1203,1225,1228],{},"Interfaces, classes (their fields, without their methods), generic instantiations such as ",[274,1212,1213],{},"Page\u003CReport>",", mapped types such as ",[274,1216,1217],{},"Partial\u003CReport>",[274,1219,1220],{},"Pick\u003CReport, 'id'>",", intersections, and unions of objects are objects, named for the type and its type arguments (",[274,1223,1224],{},"Page_Report",[274,1226,1227],{},"Partial_Report",").",[1183,1230,1231,1116,1234,1237],{},[274,1232,1233],{},"Record\u003Cstring, V>",[274,1235,1236],{},"{[key: string]: V}"," are maps, enums are enums, and a union of string literals is a string.",[1183,1239,1185,1240,1243,1244,1246,1247,1250],{},[274,1241,1242],{},"Date"," is published as a date, but it arrives as the ISO-8601 string a date travels as: the service receives a string, and a TypeScript caller gets a string back. ",[274,1245,1140],{}," logs a warning for each one, and the directory carries the same warning in the ",[274,1248,1249],{},"warnings"," metadata of the parameter, or of the function for a result.",[1183,1252,1185,1253,1203,1256,1203,1259,1203,1262,1203,1265,1268],{},[274,1254,1255],{},"Map",[274,1257,1258],{},"Set",[274,1260,1261],{},"Uint8Array",[274,1263,1264],{},"Buffer",[274,1266,1267],{},"bigint",", tuple, or function fails generation with the reason and the type to declare instead.",[282,1270,1272],{"id":1271},"decorators","Decorators",[1172,1274,1276],{"id":1275},"publishnamespace-name-advertise","@Publish(namespace?, name?, advertise?)",[270,1278,1279,1280,1283,1284,1287,1288,1291,1292,1295,1296,1299],{},"Marks a class for publication. The full service identifier becomes ",[274,1281,1282],{},"namespace.ClassName","; both parts are optional (the name defaults to the class name). A service published with no namespace is addressed by its name in its zone, ",[274,1285,1286],{},"srv:\u002F\u002F\u003Czone>~ClassName",", and the platform's service directory names it in its zone's namespace, ",[274,1289,1290],{},"\u003Czone>.ClassName",", so services of the same name in different applications stay apart. Passing ",[274,1293,1294],{},"advertise"," as ",[274,1297,1298],{},"true"," additionally advertises the service in the platform service directory, so it appears in directory listings for browsing and invocation — publishing alone makes a service callable over RPC without listing it.",[1172,1301,1303],{"id":1302},"zonezone","@Zone(zone)",[270,1305,1306,1307,1309],{},"Declares the zone the service is addressable in, relative to the client's ",[274,1308,547],{},". The zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[1172,1311,1313],{"id":1312},"versionversion","@Version(version)",[270,1315,1316,1317,1320],{},"Sets the semantic version for the service in ",[274,1318,1319],{},"X.Y.Z"," format. Callers can pin to a specific version when resolving the service.",[1172,1322,1324],{"id":1323},"scope","@Scope",[270,1326,1327],{},"A getter or method decorator that marks the member providing the scope identifier. Scope targets requests at one specific instance of a service — for example the copy running on a particular node or device.",[287,1329,1331],{"className":289,"c